config EMU
    bool "Emulator build"
    default n
    help
      Selects the emulator linker script with expanded POOL (464 KiB
      instead of 336 KiB). Enables features that need more RAM than
      real hardware has, such as the shadow framebuffer.

menu "Debug"

config DEBUG
    bool "Debug mode"
    default n
    help
      Master switch for debug features. Enables diagnostic logging,
      the DEBUG UI page, and future debug instrumentation.

config DEBUG_LOG
    bool "Debug logging"
    default y if DEBUG
    depends on DEBUG
    help
      Enable diagnostic logging via modd_log(). Lines are always
      streamed to the HW debug box (DBG_WR_EN, MMIO 0x1EEE240)
      where the emulator or a JTAG probe can capture them. The
      optional RAM ring buffer (DEBUG_LOG_BUF) keeps recent lines
      for the LCD debug page.

config DEBUG_LOG_BUF
    bool "Debug log RAM ring buffer"
    default y
    depends on DEBUG_LOG
    help
      Keep recent log lines in a RAM ring buffer so the DEBUG UI
      page can display them. Disable to save ~13-26 KB of RAM
      when only the HW debug stream is needed.

config DEBUG_LOG_LINES
    int "Log ring buffer lines"
    depends on DEBUG_LOG_BUF
    range 64 1024
    default 248
    help
      Number of lines in the debug log ring buffer.
      Each line is 48 bytes; timestamps add 4 bytes per line.
      256 = 13KB, 512 = 26KB. Increase for USB hub debugging.

config DEBUG_DAP
    bool "USB debug protocol (DAP)"
    default y if DEBUG
    depends on DEBUG && USB
    help
      Enable the fm1-dock SysEx debug protocol (D_HELLO, D_LOG).
      Adds a NOINIT byte ring buffer that survives resets; the host
      reads logs incrementally via tools/fm1log.py or hbdeploy.py.

config DEBUG_FRAMEBUFFER
    bool "Shadow framebuffer (emulator only)"
    default y if EMU
    depends on RPC && EMU
    help
      Keep a 240x240 RGB565 shadow copy of the LCD in RAM (112 KB).
      Every lcd_blit/lcd_fill also writes to this buffer, and
      GET /api/screenshot serves it as raw RGB565 (base64).
      Only enable in emulator builds where RAM is not constrained.

config MIRROR
    bool "LCD mirror over WebSocket"
    default n
    depends on RPC && LWIP
    help
      Stream the LCD to a browser via WebSocket. Hooks lcd_blit/lcd_fill,
      compresses dirty rectangles (RLE + segment hashing from fm1-base's
      mirror.c) and sends them as binary WebSocket frames. Open /mirror
      in a browser to view the screen live.
      Cost: ~11 KB RAM (segment hashes, codec buffers).
      Off in every defconfig since 2026-11-27: the WebSocket transport has
      no backpressure and its send blocks the LCD flush. See docs/features/MIRROR.md.

endmenu
